  "plan": {
    "hardest_frame": 5,
    "visual_argument": "Every count is drawn as units a reader can count at one stated scale, a box for a million flies a week, a windmill for a premises, an animal for a thousand seen, while the camera climbs a scale ladder from a fly on a fence wire to a region and back down to a trailer and a gate the models can't see.",
    "build_risk": "The Edinburg apron must read as a place, 80 boxes in 100 painted slots with a 300 outline at the same pitch and a worker for size, never as bars. The cover's fly is the hardest single model, built in the chassis from primitives at true size.",
    "distinct_from_recent": "No. 53 was nine material reliefs of a tissue section with type in a top band every frame. This deck stages seven exterior scenes and two reliefs with the type moving. No. 52 was nightSodium and a robotaxi; this is lastLight brush country with no vehicle hero. No. 51 was a lastLight courtroom with tiny figures on dead floor; here every subject fills a third to two thirds of the frame and the lower third carries ground, contact and texture."
  },
